            <ArticleTitle>Late acute thrombosis after coronary brachytherapy: when is the risk over?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>216-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Late total occlusion (LTO) after simultaneous coronary stenting and brachytherapy has been described in recent randomized trials. We report a case of LTO presenting with an acute clinical event 15 months after the index procedure, suggesting that the risk is not confined to the first 6-month to 1-year period.</AbstractText>
